<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

''HIGH — Remote URL still comes from lane-controlled Git config.'' [[`commit-relay.mjs:42`|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/commit-relay.mjs:42]] defaults `remoteUrl` to `git remote get-url origin`. The allowlist in [[`seat-broker.mjs:413-426`|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/seat-broker.mjs:413]] permits lane-chosen SSH, HTTPS, and absolute paths. A lane can redirect the authorized push to an attacker’s server or a local repository; a local receiver may run its hooks. Require a controller-supplied URL.

''HIGH — Hardlinks can expose the check key through `readSafe`.'' [[`seat-broker.mjs:231-240`|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/seat-broker.mjs:231]] rejects symlinks but accepts regular files with multiple hardlinks. A lane can hardlink a same-owner key into its worktree; the descriptor path check still sees the in-worktree name. Reading or committing that file exposes the key and permits forged receipts.

''MED — Receipts can replay across changed check definitions.'' [[`seat-walls.mjs:55-59`|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/seat-walls.mjs:55]] signs the tree and check names, not check argv or configuration; [[`seat-broker.mjs:260-274`|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/seat-harness/wt/tools/seat-broker.mjs:260]] accepts that receipt when names match. A receipt from an earlier, weaker definition with the same name can satisfy updated checks.

The listed fixes otherwise hold: the throwaway repo avoids lane push config and source hooks; alternates still expose Git’s object database as data, not executable lane files. The empty-dir bind hides the protected controller directory. `--ignore-pnpmfile` covers config-dependency hooks; workspace YAML and legacy `package.json` pnpm fields can affect install configuration, but do not by themselves execute hooks with scripts disabled ([[pnpm install docs|https://pnpm.io/cli/install]]).

<<~/ahu>>

